EXPERIMENT-4.1 MIDDLE OF LINKED LIST(QUESTION-876 LEETCODE)
AIM:-Given the head of a singly linked list, return the middle node of the linked list.If there are two middle nodes, return the second middle node.
ALGORITHM:-
1. Start with the head of the linked list.
2. Take two pointers: slow and fast, both starting from the head.
3. Move the slow pointer one step at a time.
4. Move the fast pointer two steps at a time.
5. Continue this process until the fast pointer reaches the end of the list.
6. When the fast pointer reaches the end, the slow pointer will be at the middle.
7. Return the node pointed to by slow.
CODE:-
class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* middleNode(ListNode* head) {
        ListNode*slow=head;
        ListNode*fast=head;
        while(fast!=nullptr&&fast->next!=nullptr){
            slow=slow->next;
            fast=fast->next->next;
        }
        return slow;
    }
};

EXPERIMENT-4.2 PALIDROME OF LINKEDLIST (QUESTION-234 LEETCODE)
AIM:-Given the head of a singly linked list, return true if it is a palindrome or false otherwise.
ALGORITHM :-
1. Create an empty stack s1.
2. Set temp = head to start from the first node.
3. Traverse the linked list:
     - Push each node's value into the stack.
     - Move temp to the next node.
4. Reset temp = head.
5. Traverse the linked list again:
      - Compare temp->val with the value at the top of the stack.
      - If they are different, return false.
      - If they are same, remove the top element using pop().
      - Move temp to the next node.
6. If all values match, return true.
7. Therefore, the linked list is a palindrome
CODE:-class Solution {
public:
    bool isPalindrome(ListNode* head) {
        stack<int>s1;
        ListNode* temp=head;
        while(temp!=NULL){
            s1.push(temp->val);
            temp=temp->next;
        }
         temp=head;
        while(temp!=NULL){
            if(temp->val!=s1.top()){
                return false;
            }
            s1.pop();
            temp=temp->next;
        }
        return true;
    }
};
